# Null-test case for the ASSIGN golden (Story 4.10): assign.liveset (an organ, ASSIGN map K1 = drawbar 4', K2 = reverb send, K3 empty) played by assign.mid with
# --assign-mode and the encoder turns of CMakeLists.txt (a drawbar and the reverb send moving during a held chord; K3 is empty and does nothing).
# -100 dB residual: far below the audible effect of the encoders, loose enough for libm/FMA differences between macOS and Linux builds.
# check_excess: a tail in one file only fails as well.
reference=assign.wav
tolerance_db=-100
max_offset_frames=0
max_length_diff_frames=0
check_excess=1
